WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.299 --> 00:00:05.210
Sometimes certain situations in life have
you wishing for a quick way out.

00:00:05.210 --> 00:00:09.410
Waiting to have a meeting with your boss,
heading into an important test, or getting

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:14.290
ready to have an awkward conversation with
a romantic partner who just texted that “we

00:00:14.290 --> 00:00:15.410
need to talk”.

00:00:15.410 --> 00:00:17.970
All of these can be pretty hard to deal with.

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.689
In times like these, it can be easy to want
to run away.

00:00:21.689 --> 00:00:25.749
We feel a part of ourselves saying that it
would be better to just bail out as quickly

00:00:25.749 --> 00:00:26.970
as we can.

00:00:26.970 --> 00:00:31.119
But just because choosing to make an exit
is often the quickest way to avoid a problem,

00:00:31.119 --> 00:00:36.110
that doesn’t always mean it’s the best
solution - especially when your means of escape

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:39.460
venture into the world of the anomalous.

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:43.510
Sometimes you have to face things head on,
but if you are still really in need of a quick

00:00:43.510 --> 00:00:48.620
way out, then SCP-120 might just be what you
are looking for.

00:00:48.620 --> 00:00:50.850
But don’t say we didn’t warn you.

00:00:50.850 --> 00:00:52.300
Now, hear us out.

00:00:52.300 --> 00:00:55.559
Yes, we know that it’s a children’s paddling
pool.

00:00:55.559 --> 00:00:58.350
You might have even owned one yourself back
in the day.

00:00:58.350 --> 00:01:02.560
When the warm summer months came rolling around,
your younger self would have begged your poor

00:01:02.560 --> 00:01:07.390
parents to spend several minutes in the sun’s
glaring heat, breathlessly inflating a pool

00:01:07.390 --> 00:01:10.800
just like it, then filling it with water from
the garden hose.

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:15.360
All so you could put on your water wings,
have a splash around for an hour or two, then

00:01:15.360 --> 00:01:17.290
go inside to dry off.

00:01:17.290 --> 00:01:18.570
The result?

00:01:18.570 --> 00:01:22.670
Leaving the water in that paddling pool to
go stagnant as it got left outside in the

00:01:22.670 --> 00:01:27.700
summer sun, filled with dirt, leaves, and
mosquito larvae while you decided that air

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:32.180
conditioning and Super Mario was a better
way to spend your time.

00:01:32.180 --> 00:01:38.900
But SCP-120, as will likely come as no surprise,
is no ordinary children’s paddling pool.

00:01:38.900 --> 00:01:44.251
Sure, it might look like an ordinary paddling
pool at first: Pastel pink in color, only

00:01:44.251 --> 00:01:48.110
two and a half meters in diameter, and less
than a meter tall.

00:01:48.110 --> 00:01:52.700
It’s even made out of that same typical
flimsy plastic that needs to be inflated with

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:54.500
air to hold a shape.

00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:57.570
You know, the kind that absorbed all that
heat from the sunlight while your younger

00:01:57.570 --> 00:02:02.240
self was out there splashing around, just
waiting to burn your skin at the slightest

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:03.240
touch.

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:07.970
But the first key difference between SCP-120
and the pool you had while you were growing

00:02:07.970 --> 00:02:12.230
up is, well, this one is indestructible.

00:02:12.230 --> 00:02:17.910
Despite being made from common Earth plastics,
SCP-120 cannot be damaged or destroyed by

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:19.880
any conventional means.

00:02:19.880 --> 00:02:24.120
Though the material it is made from will still
flex when pressure is applied, and is soft

00:02:24.120 --> 00:02:28.340
to the touch, it also possesses an anomalous
tensile strength.

00:02:28.340 --> 00:02:33.810
In other words, SCP-120 cannot be ripped,
stretched, or otherwise destroyed like an

00:02:33.810 --> 00:02:35.800
ordinary paddling pool can.

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:40.170
And the SCP Foundation would know, they’ve
destroyed their own fair share of paddling

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:42.110
pools in the research labs.

00:02:42.110 --> 00:02:47.530
Okay, so SCP-120 is an indestructible child’s
paddling pool, surely there has to be more

00:02:47.530 --> 00:02:48.880
to it than that?

00:02:48.880 --> 00:02:52.850
Otherwise, why would it be such an important
object to the SCP Foundation?

00:02:52.850 --> 00:02:56.740
Well, you’re right, there’s much more
to it than that.

00:02:56.740 --> 00:03:01.350
After all, they don’t call it the Teleporting
Paddling Pool for nothing.

00:03:01.350 --> 00:03:06.880
Within the pool itself is a glowing substance,
almost like a liquid but somehow unlike any

00:03:06.880 --> 00:03:10.030
in existence, at least in this dimension.

00:03:10.030 --> 00:03:11.790
What exactly do we mean by that?

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:16.040
Well, this “liquid” doesn’t behave in
quite the same way you would expect from,

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:20.910
say, water, for example, and its physical
properties don’t align with the rules of

00:03:20.910 --> 00:03:21.910
our universe.

00:03:21.910 --> 00:03:26.069
Let’s say, you fill your ordinary paddling
pool with water, just like you would have

00:03:26.069 --> 00:03:28.270
done on a hot summer day as a kid.

00:03:28.270 --> 00:03:32.370
Now, because of the properties of the water,
you know you could easily grab a drinking

00:03:32.370 --> 00:03:36.150
glass from your kitchen cabinet and fill it
up from the pool no problem.

00:03:36.150 --> 00:03:41.750
However, the substance within SCP-120 does
not obey these same rules, you simply cannot

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:46.010
grab a glass or other container and scoop
up some of this glowing liquid.

00:03:46.010 --> 00:03:47.170
See what we mean?

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:51.420
The “liquid” is only really a liquid in
name and can’t be manipulated in the same

00:03:51.420 --> 00:03:53.840
way that an ordinary liquid can.

00:03:53.840 --> 00:03:58.240
However, it does also share the appearance
of being a liquid, with its surface rippling

00:03:58.240 --> 00:04:00.360
and shimmering often as it moves.

00:04:00.360 --> 00:04:03.650
So, put all of that together and what is the
conclusion you get?

00:04:03.650 --> 00:04:09.099
That this substance definitely does not exist
in our own dimension, instead it is from somewhere

00:04:09.099 --> 00:04:10.800
else entirely.

00:04:10.800 --> 00:04:16.789
By far the biggest difference between SCP-120
and any ordinary pastel pink colored WalMart

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:20.859
paddling pool is the property that the Foundation
is most interested in.

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:26.210
In fact, this paddling pool is part of that
oh-so-rare category of SCPs that actually

00:04:26.210 --> 00:04:32.330
have a practical use, thanks to this anomalous
property: Human beings, along with the clothes

00:04:32.330 --> 00:04:36.819
they’re wearing and any items they might
be carrying, will be teleported to one of

00:04:36.819 --> 00:04:40.529
eleven different locations should they fall
into the paddling pool.

00:04:40.529 --> 00:04:44.789
To reiterate, they don’t call it the Teleporting
Paddling Pool for nothing.

00:04:44.789 --> 00:04:49.449
There are some small limitations to SCP-120’s
teleportation ability.

00:04:49.449 --> 00:04:54.050
For one, the weight of objects or loads being
carried through it by one person cannot exceed

00:04:54.050 --> 00:04:59.860
the maximum threshold of just under thirty
eight kilos, or almost eighty four pounds.

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:05.220
There are also only eleven destinations that
SCP-120 can send someone to, and these can’t

00:05:05.220 --> 00:05:08.580
be pre-programmed or predetermined beforehand.

00:05:08.580 --> 00:05:13.110
Any subjects stepping into the pool must be
conscious, carrying weight under the specified

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:18.240
amount, be biologically a human being and
can only use the Teleporting Paddling Pool

00:05:18.240 --> 00:05:20.189
one person at a time.

00:05:20.189 --> 00:05:23.879
Meeting these requirements means that the
pool will work as expected.

00:05:23.879 --> 00:05:28.620
The only repercussion of not meeting the aforementioned
criteria is simply that the pool will not

00:05:28.620 --> 00:05:29.660
function.

00:05:29.660 --> 00:05:33.629
Any who have stepped into the pool carrying
too much weight for example, have merely reported

00:05:33.629 --> 00:05:37.309
that their feet touch the surface beneath
the glowing ‘liquid’.

00:05:37.309 --> 00:05:44.189
First encountered by the SCP Foundation in
September 1992, SCP-120 was found in California

00:05:44.189 --> 00:05:47.540
following reports of children going missing
in the area.

00:05:47.540 --> 00:05:52.680
There they discovered the Teleporting Paddling
Pool, and brought it back to Site 19 for testing.

00:05:52.680 --> 00:05:57.569
It is currently unknown how many children
went missing, or if they were ever recovered.

00:05:57.569 --> 00:06:01.759
Regardless, remember how we talked about making
a quick exit at the start of this video?

00:06:01.759 --> 00:06:06.469
Well, that’s because the Foundation’s
biggest interest in SCP-120 was to use it

00:06:06.469 --> 00:06:11.479
as a means of rapid evacuation for their most
important group of people - the Overwatch

00:06:11.479 --> 00:06:14.979
Command, also known as the O5 Council.

00:06:14.979 --> 00:06:19.400
During a major emergency like a containment
breach, the O5s would use the paddling pool

00:06:19.400 --> 00:06:21.240
to escape to safety.

00:06:21.240 --> 00:06:25.789
As you may have already gathered from how
we’ve described it, SCP-120 has the inert

00:06:25.789 --> 00:06:29.919
ability to instantly relocate a person from
one place to another.

00:06:29.919 --> 00:06:34.680
According to the theories of the SCP Foundation’s
researchers, it likely does this by allowing

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:39.029
the subject to pass through one or more dimensions
alternate to our own.

00:06:39.029 --> 00:06:43.809
We also mentioned that one of the limits of
SCP-120 is that it can only send someone to

00:06:43.809 --> 00:06:46.430
one of eleven different places.

00:06:46.430 --> 00:06:51.159
These are distinguished by the liquid-like
substance contained in SCP-120 undergoing

00:06:51.159 --> 00:06:52.550
a change of color.

00:06:52.550 --> 00:06:57.560
By sending disposable members of D Class personnel
carrying radio beacons through, the Foundation

00:06:57.560 --> 00:07:02.509
has been able to compile a list of these destinations,
and they are as follows:

00:07:02.509 --> 00:07:08.559
The first of these is the Pacific Ocean, denoted
by a blue glow of SCP-120’s liquid.

00:07:08.559 --> 00:07:12.740
When traveling here, subjects are deposited
around two meters above the surface of the

00:07:12.740 --> 00:07:13.770
Pacific.

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:19.110
Since this location was discovered during
testing, a Foundation vessel named the SCPS

00:07:19.110 --> 00:07:22.000
Demeter has been stationed at these coordinates.

00:07:22.000 --> 00:07:26.210
To the public, this ship is known instead
as the USS Nassau, operating under the cover

00:07:26.210 --> 00:07:28.979
story of being a simple meteorological boat.

00:07:28.979 --> 00:07:31.460
But why would the Foundation leave a boat
here?

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:34.979
The current position of this ship means that
anyone traveling to the Pacific through the

00:07:34.979 --> 00:07:38.970
Teleporting Paddling Pool will appear in the
vessel’s cargo hold.

00:07:38.970 --> 00:07:43.120
In a crisis, important personnel could be
sent to the Demeter, and the boat could even

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:48.960
be used to hold less dangerous SCP objects,
if they could be sent through SCP-120.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:54.659
Of course, teleporting oneself aboard a boat
might be a bit trickier, say, during a storm.

00:07:54.659 --> 00:07:58.580
If the Demeter is moved too far from its current
position, there’s a chance someone might

00:07:58.580 --> 00:08:02.020
end up teleporting inside one of the ship’s
walls.

00:08:02.020 --> 00:08:07.990
The next location is Greenland, where SCP-120
will send someone when its liquid glows white.

00:08:07.990 --> 00:08:12.240
Arriving here, one will find themself in a
facility that the Foundation has established

00:08:12.240 --> 00:08:13.340
on site.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:17.129
The cover story for this one is that this
building is part of an expansion of the oil

00:08:17.129 --> 00:08:18.129
industry.

00:08:18.129 --> 00:08:22.369
What members of the public are not privy to
is the true function of the facility.

00:08:22.369 --> 00:08:26.599
The Foundation set this site up specifically
to perform the same function as their ship

00:08:26.599 --> 00:08:27.599
the Demeter.

00:08:27.599 --> 00:08:32.669
The facility even has an airstrip and a refueling
station there, meaning any who use the paddling

00:08:32.669 --> 00:08:37.130
pool to teleport to Greenland can further
relocate themselves aboard a Foundation aircraft

00:08:37.130 --> 00:08:38.459
if necessary.

00:08:38.459 --> 00:08:43.829
If the liquid in SCP-120 ever changes to become
a deep black in color, it will then lead to

00:08:43.829 --> 00:08:47.819
one of five possible points that are all practically
identical.

00:08:47.819 --> 00:08:51.230
These destinations are various Earth-Moon
Lagrange Points.

00:08:51.230 --> 00:08:55.779
In celestial mechanics, a Lagrange Point is
an area near two large bodies orbiting in

00:08:55.779 --> 00:08:56.779
space.

00:08:56.779 --> 00:09:01.329
To put it in simple terms, in this case, these
are points between the Earth and the Moon

00:09:01.329 --> 00:09:04.899
where the gravitational forces of both balance
each other out.

00:09:04.899 --> 00:09:09.690
This is what makes these Lagrange Points such
good locations for satellites, as the equal

00:09:09.690 --> 00:09:14.069
forces make it easier for a satellite to achieve
the right path of orbit.

00:09:14.069 --> 00:09:18.930
So, objects or people sent through SCP-120
when the water blackens will end up at either

00:09:18.930 --> 00:09:23.680
Lagrange Point 1, 2, 3, 4 or 5.

00:09:23.680 --> 00:09:27.509
These points are located all the way around
the Earth, and are directly between the Earth

00:09:27.509 --> 00:09:31.250
and the Moon whenever the latter makes its
orbit around the former.

00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:35.060
Essentially, jumping through the Teleporting
Paddling Pool when it has been “dialed”

00:09:35.060 --> 00:09:40.100
to one of these locations is like taking the
high dive into the cold, endless vacuum of

00:09:40.100 --> 00:09:44.150
space, ending up lost forever, impossible
to retrieve.

00:09:44.150 --> 00:09:49.769
The SCP Foundation plans to potentially use
these SCP-120 destinations to dispose of anomalous

00:09:49.769 --> 00:09:54.649
objects during a crisis, as a way to prevent
them from falling into the wrong hands.

00:09:54.649 --> 00:09:59.089
Now, we mentioned that SCP-120’s “liquid”
will glow white when it’s linked to the

00:09:59.089 --> 00:10:03.410
destination in Greenland, but the same also
occurs when it is dialed to the snow capped

00:10:03.410 --> 00:10:05.350
mountains of the Himalayas.

00:10:05.350 --> 00:10:09.810
This famous mountain range in Southern and
Eastern Asia is home to a number of Planet

00:10:09.810 --> 00:10:11.850
Earth’s tallest peaks.

00:10:11.850 --> 00:10:16.279
Most notably Mount Everest, the highest mountain
in the world, resting at the border between

00:10:16.279 --> 00:10:18.029
Nepal and China.

00:10:18.029 --> 00:10:21.579
Unlike some of the other destinations, the
Foundation has made little change to this

00:10:21.579 --> 00:10:22.579
one.

00:10:22.579 --> 00:10:27.410
No boats or bases for anyone to materialize
into safety have been designated to the area.

00:10:27.410 --> 00:10:31.620
Instead, there’s just an eight meter hole
where the bodies of D Class test subjects

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:35.440
have been disposed of, hidden from view by
a canopy.

00:10:35.440 --> 00:10:40.360
Only in extreme cases would the O5 Council
ever want to evacuate to here.

00:10:40.360 --> 00:10:45.170
Should SCP-120 display a yellow glow, then
someone traveling through it will arrive in

00:10:45.170 --> 00:10:47.310
the Sahara Desert, in Africa.

00:10:47.310 --> 00:10:52.490
The Sahara is famous for being the largest
hot desert in the entire world, only beaten

00:10:52.490 --> 00:10:56.410
in size by the northern Arctic and Antarctic
deserts.

00:10:56.410 --> 00:11:00.649
Located here is a much smaller Foundation
installation, an outpost that would most likely

00:11:00.649 --> 00:11:06.360
be ineffective for housing anomalous objects,
but in an evacuation could prove a useful

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:11.860
hiding place for important SCP documents,
or even for members of the Overwatch Command.

00:11:11.860 --> 00:11:17.639
If SCP-120 produces a brown glow in its liquid,
it will transport a subject to the Gobi Desert,

00:11:17.639 --> 00:11:22.610
a region in northern China and southern Mongolia
famous for its unique ecosystem.

00:11:22.610 --> 00:11:28.490
Here, much like the Sahara location, the Foundation
has established an identical small outpost.

00:11:28.490 --> 00:11:34.780
However, this one does come with the threat
of another anomaly, SCP-4024.

00:11:34.780 --> 00:11:39.760
This is a saltwater spring that is gradually
expanding across the Gobi, which, much like

00:11:39.760 --> 00:11:45.370
the Teleporting Paddling Pool, has the ability
to displace people and objects to an unknown

00:11:45.370 --> 00:11:46.370
location.

00:11:46.370 --> 00:11:51.129
Finally, should SCP-120 ever emit a subdued,
gray-colored glow, traveling through it will

00:11:51.129 --> 00:11:53.389
lead to an area in the Sea of Rains.

00:11:53.389 --> 00:11:57.470
But that’s not a sea on Earth, that’s
on the Moon.

00:11:57.470 --> 00:12:01.310
And it’s not so much a “sea” as it is
a vast plain.

00:12:01.310 --> 00:12:05.220
Luckily, if you were to end up here, the Foundation
has already thought ahead and set up a station

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.610
on the lunar surface, and it’s thought to
be one of their safest.

00:12:08.610 --> 00:12:13.339
So, at least if the Teleporting Paddling Pool
sent you to the moon, you would be able to

00:12:13.339 --> 00:12:14.339
survive.

00:12:14.339 --> 00:12:15.420
That’s reassuring.

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:18.600
Of course, the real problem is, how do you
get back home?

00:12:18.600 --> 00:12:21.300
That’s a question for another day.

00:12:21.300 --> 00:12:24.970
Just like we told you at the start of this
video, sometimes it’s better to just face

00:12:24.970 --> 00:12:31.230
your problems head-on, because certain escapes
can lead to more complications than you bargained

00:12:31.230 --> 00:12:32.230
for.

00:12:32.230 --> 00:12:39.089
Now go check out “Minecraft World Destroyer
SCP-4335 - A Welt In The Crucible” and “SCP-5094

00:12:39.089 --> 00:12:44.220
- Miss J's Whiz Kidz Schoolhouse” for more
SCPs that put the strange into your childhood

00:12:44.220 --> 00:12:44.750
joys!

